-- title:
--   Elements of an affine blow-up chart are g/a^N with g ∈ J^N
-- statement:
--   Let $C$ be a commutative ring and $K$ a field equipped with a $C$-algebra structure, with structure map $\mathrm{algebraMap}\,C\,K$. Let $J \subseteq C$ be an ideal and let $a \in J$ be an element whose image in $K$ is non-zero. Let $x \in K$ belong to the $C$-subalgebra of $K$ generated by the set of those $y \in K$ for which there exists $i \in J$ with $y \cdot \mathrm{algebraMap}\,C\,K\,a = \mathrm{algebraMap}\,C\,K\,i$, that is, by the elements of $K$ that become an element of $J$ after multiplication by the image of $a$. The conclusion is that there exist a natural number $N$ and an element $g \in J^N$ with $x \cdot (\mathrm{algebraMap}\,C\,K\,a)^N = \mathrm{algebraMap}\,C\,K\,g$; thus every element of this subalgebra is of the form $g/a^N$ with $g \in J^N$.
--
--   This is the standard description of the affine blow-up algebra $C[J/a] = \sum_N J^N a^{-N}$ realised inside a field: the chart of the blow-up of $\operatorname{Spec} C$ along $J$ where the generator $a$ of $J$ is inverted. It is used in the analysis of the blow-up charts occurring in the auxiliary level structures on modular curves, where it supplies the inclusion needed for the contraction identity $J^n = C \cap a^n C[J/a]$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Algebra_exists_pow_mem_mul_pow_eq_of_mem_adjoin_blowupChart.lean

